      "problem": "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = x\\sec x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x) \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x+x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1+x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
